Subject: [PATCH] README: Document --cache-path and --submount-cache

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 README.md | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2a4c843..b7cbbf8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -263,6 +263,26 @@ The caching policy the file system should use (auto, always, metadata, never).
 
 Default: auto.
 
+```shell
+--cache-path <PATH=POLICY>
+```
+Cache policy for mounts at or below PATH within the shared directory (repeatable).  PATH is absolute, relative to the
+shared directory, and is normalised lexically (`//`, `.`, `..` and a trailing `/`); it must not lead outside the shared
+directory, and need not exist or be a mount point.  A mount found within the shared directory, at any time, takes the
+policy of the longest PATH that is its mount point or a parent directory of it (`/a` covers `/a` and `/a/b`, not `/ab`);
+the order of the options does not matter.  Mount points are matched by their real paths, so a PATH through a symbolic
+link never matches (virtiofsd warns about one that exists at startup).  A mount's policy is decided when virtiofsd first
+sees it; a mount later moved with `mount --move` keeps it.  Requires mount IDs (Linux 5.8); unique mount IDs (Linux 6.8)
+let virtiofsd remember each mount's policy instead of looking it up again.
+
+```shell
+--submount-cache <POLICY>
+```
+Cache policy for every mount within the shared directory, other than the shared directory's own, that no `--cache-path`
+covers.
+
+Default: the `--cache` policy.
+
 ```shell
 --allow-mmap
 ```
